---
title: "5 · Start a case from the template"
description: Start a case from the template on the Cases board and check the tasks it creates.
sidebar:
  order: 6
  label: "5 · Start a case from the template"
---

**Who:** a manager or admin of the department that owns the template, or a partner. A tenant admin who is not in that department cannot start one either. Other users see **+ New Case** greyed out; hover over the button to read the reason. **Where:** the department workspace › **Cases**.

## New case

{% steps %}

1. Select **+ New Case**.
2. Leave **Case title** blank to name the case automatically from the case type and the client, or enter a title.
3. In **Case type**, choose the template, for example `Sample Client Onboarding`.
4. In **Assigned to**, choose the person in charge, for example Demo Manager.
5. In **Client**, choose the client, for example ABC PTE. LTD. The client is required when **Needs a client** is on in the template.
6. In **Start**, choose the start date. If you leave **Due** blank, the case due date is worked out from the template's **Default case length** (in this example, 10 business days after the start).
7. Select **Create Case**.

{% /steps %}

{% screenshot id="case-templates/case-new" caption="The New Case dialog." /%}

## The case on the board

The case appears in the **Ready to start** column. Its progress shows how many tasks are done, for example `0/6`.

{% screenshot id="case-templates/case-board" caption="The new case on the Cases board." /%}

## The Tasks tab

Open the case and select the **Tasks** tab:

- The template is expanded into its sections and tasks.
- The due dates are worked out as calendar dates.
- A section that must wait for an earlier section shows what it is waiting on. To begin it early, select **Start anyway**.

{% screenshot id="case-templates/case-tasks" caption="The Tasks tab of a case started from the template." /%}

{% aside type="note" title="Cases opened from a contract" %}
A case that a signed contract opens, or that is started with **Start case** on a contract service, uses the case type set for that service in the service catalog, not a type chosen in **New Case**. If the service has prerequisites, the case shows a **Prerequisites** checklist and stays with the opportunity owner until every item is satisfied; on **My Week** it is marked **Pre-start checklist · Waiting on you**. Prerequisites are set on the service, not in the case template.
{% /aside %}
